  "finalText": "Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n**Bug trace across layers:**\n1. `POST /api/auth/logout` → `authenticate` middleware → `authService.verifyToken(token)` → **returns cached user from `verifiedCache`** (line 94)\n2. Route handler → `authService.logout(token)` → only calls `sessionRepository.delete(token)` — **DB row deleted, but `verifiedCache` not cleared**\n3. Next request with same JWT → `verifyToken` finds token still in `verifiedCache` → returns user → **all protected endpoints accept stale identity**\n\n**Root cause** at `src/services/authService.ts:8-10`: A module-level `Map<string, UserModel>` cached verified tokens but `logout()` never invalidated entries. Even clearing the cache wasn't enough because the JWT remains cryptographically valid — `verifyToken` would re-verify and re-cache on the next request.\n\n**Fix (3 changes in `src/services/authService.ts`):**\n1. Added `revokedTokens` set (line 9) — `logout()` adds the token (line 67)\n2. `verifyToken()` checks `revokedTokens` first (line 95-97) — throws `401 \"Token has been revoked\"` before cache/DB lookup\n3. `changePassword()` also revokes all cached tokens for the user (line 136)\n\n**Test** (`tests/auth.test.ts`): Two new tests in `logout revocation`:\n- Verifies `verifyToken` throws after `logout` for the same token\n- Verifies the `authenticate` middleware returns 401 on all 22 protected paths after logout",
